\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Accounting for Intensity Techniques and Overlapping Slots\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When logging specialized intensity techniques, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  enforces a maximum set credit cap per exercise entry to prevent arbitrary volume inflation. A single exercise slot utilizing rest-pause or drop sets cannot exceed $1.50$ total effective sets toward the primary target muscle.\
For multi-slot exercise configurations occurring within a single workout session (such as two distinct back pulling movements performed during a single Pull session), each completed working set credits the primary target muscle fully. However, to prevent acute intra-session fatigue from generating unproductive "junk volume," total primary set volume per muscle group is capped at $8.0\\text\{--\}10.0$ effective sets per session. Any working set completed beyond $10.0$ effective sets for a single muscle group in one session yields a decayed stimulus credit of $0.50$ effective sets in the weekly ledger, reflecting intra-session diminishing returns.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Muscle Contribution Model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 Fractional Set Accounting Framework\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Traditional binary set counting\'97assigning $1.0$ set to all involved muscles or $1.0$ set only to the primary muscle\'97introduces systemic programming errors. Binary counting either over-prescribes secondary isolation work or omits the substantial hypertrophic stimulus received by synergist muscles during heavy compound movements.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  utilizes a fractional set mapping model supported by multi-level meta-regressions. Compound movements assign primary movers $1.00$ set credit, major synergists $0.50$ set credit, and minor stabilisers $0.25$ or $0.00$ set credit.\
$$\\text\{Effective Weekly Volume \} (V_\{\\text\{eff\}, m\}) = \\sum S_\{\\text\{direct\}, m\} + \\sum \\left( \\omega_\{i, m\} \\cdot S_\{\\text\{indirect\}, i\} \\right)$$\
In this equation, $S_\{\\text\{direct\}, m\}$ represents the count of direct working sets for muscle group $m$, $S_\{\\text\{indirect\}, i\}$ represents the count of working sets performed on compound exercise $i$, and $\\omega_\{i, m\} \\in \\\{0.50, 0.25\\\}$ defines the primary-to-synergist contribution coefficient.\

