\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Synergist Caps and Target Protection Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 To prevent fractional volume from masking a complete lack of direct isolation stimulus (for example, performing 20 sets of heavy rows and accumulating $10.0$ fractional sets for biceps without executing a direct curl), 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  enforces two deterministic rules:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Synergist Contribution Ceiling
\f1\b0 : Indirect fractional sets ($\\sum \\omega_\{i, m\} \\cdot S_\{\\text\{indirect\}, i\}$) can satisfy a maximum of $50\\%$ of a muscle group's total weekly Target Volume ($V_\{\\text\{target\}\}$). The remaining $50\\%$ must be supplied by direct isolation or primary mover sets ($S_\{\\text\{direct\}\} = 1.00$).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Direct Floor Minimum
\f1\b0 : If a muscle group's weekly MEV target is $\\ge 8.0$ sets, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  mandates a hard minimum floor of at least $4.0$ direct sets ($S_\{\\text\{direct\}\}$) per week allocated to dedicated primary pattern slots.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Landmark Seed, Refinement, and Reseed Specification\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 Base Volume Landmarks across Demographic Priors\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Volume landmarks\'97Minimum Effective Volume (MEV), Maximum Adaptive Volume (MAV), and Maximum Recoverable Volume (MRV)\'97vary based on muscle architecture, recovery capacity, and training experience. Global scalar multipliers (such as multiplying all muscle groups by $0.85$ for novices) introduce errors because smaller muscle groups and intermediate lifters exhibit non-linear volume tolerances.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  establishes muscle-specific baseline volume landmarks (measured in total effective weekly sets) for intermediate lifters, applying demographic modifiers based on empirical recovery capacity.\

