\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Mid-Block Reseed Policy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When a user modifies profile parameters (such as changing experience level or training template) mid-mesocycle, 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  executes a non-destructive landmark recalculation:\
Completed sets and historical week targets within the active mesocycle remain unchanged in the ledger to preserve historical tracking. Uncompleted weekly targets ($V_\{\\text\{target\}, w\}$) for remaining weeks $w \\in \\\{w_\{\\text\{current\}\}, \\dots, w_\{\\text\{final\}\}\\\}$ are updated using the ratio of the new landmark ceiling to the old landmark ceiling:\
$$V_\{\\text\{target\}, w\}^\{\\text\{new\}\} = V_\{\\text\{target\}, w\}^\{\\text\{old\}\} \\times \\left( \\frac\{\\text\{MRV\}^\{\\text\{new\}\}\}\{\\text\{MRV\}^\{\\text\{old\}\}\} \\right)$$\
Rescaled weekly targets are clamped to fall within $[\\text\{MEV\}^\{\\text\{new\}\}, \\text\{MRV\}^\{\\text\{new\}\}]$.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Autoregulated Landmark Refinement Engine\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Landmarks adjust dynamically based on logged biofeedback. 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 PlanKit
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  processes three weekly input vectors per muscle group: Average Logged RIR Delta ($\\Delta \\text\{RIR\}$, the difference between prescribed RIR and actual performed RIR), Perceived Soreness Score ($S$, an integer scale from $0$ to $4$ where $0 =$ None, $1 =$ Healed rapidly, $2 =$ Healed just in time, $3 =$ Sore upon entering session, $4 =$ Severe debilitating soreness), and Performance Trend ($\\Delta \\text\{e1RM\}$, the percentage change in estimated $1\\text\{RM\}$ on key indicator lifts over a 2-week rolling window).\

