\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Execution Algorithms\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Standard Double Progression maintains load static ($W$) while expanding repetitions performed across working sets until reaching the upper boundary of the rep range ($R_\{\\text\{max\}\}$) at target RIR. Once all prescribed sets hit $R_\{\\text\{max\}\}$, the working load increments by Load Step Size ($\\Delta W$) for the subsequent session, resetting reps to $R_\{\\text\{min\}\}$.\
Rep-First Step Progression keeps load static ($W$) while adding reps set-by-set. When Set 1 reaches $R_\{\\text\{max\}\}$, reps are added to Set 2 in subsequent sessions. Load increases only when every set achieves $R_\{\\text\{max\}\}$ at or below prescribed RIR.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

